The attitude angles, as observed in the plots, exhibit rapid and aggressive changes - effectively running on overdrive -to maintain accurate trajectory tracking. This behavior is a clear indicator of the controller’s robustness, demonstrating its ability to handle reasonable external disturbances while preserving tracking performance. To further challenge and validate the controller, an additional test case was conducted where artificial noise was introduced into the sensor measurements. This setup simulates more realistic operational conditions, ensuring that the controller not only withstands environmental disturbances but also remains resilient against measurement uncertainties.




